                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3691/47.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé McCreery to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-02-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Acknowledges department’s telegram of the 11th instant, and states that the
                    President of Mexico has telegraphed to the Presidents of Nicaragua and Honduras
                    in like sense. Says that the President of Mexico has informed Presidents of
                    Guatemala, Salvador, and Costa Rica of action taken by the United States and
                    Mexico and has invited them to take like action.</p>
            </div>
